45417] [17592186074810 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074810 #edb/ref 1061 6313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074810 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b90a454-8f0b-5456-8a77-9e48ff540512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074810 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074811 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074811 #edb/ref 1061 6314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074811 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9bd87e6f-f3bd-54dc-b78a-3a14a3f1b4c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074811 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074812 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074812 #edb/ref 1061 6315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074812 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0091640-9e7c-5a24-a5fc-74683d8bd89a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074812 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074813 #edb/ref 1061 6316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074813 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "289d8995-9823-5fd4-83fd-0b16670d28ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074813 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074949 #edb/ref 1064 "The method of subtracting fractions and whole numbers is very similar to the one we use for addition.\n\nFor example, suppose that we want to find the value of\n\n$$\n2-\\dfrac{5}{\\color{blue}6}\n$$\n\nWe first write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $\\color{blue}6$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by ${\\color{blue}{6}}$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2 \\times {\\color{blue}{6}}}{1\\times{\\color{blue}{6}}} = \\dfrac{12}{6}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\dfrac{12}{6}}_{2} - \\dfrac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same.\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{6} - \\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{7}{6}\n$$\n\nSo our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 7 {6}\n$$\n\nWe can always check our answer using a fraction model:\n\n![](images/e6/e67c582daf0ab40f08c2445b1f0527e4316d61114d12ce1aa56ede6c26f3b3a1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074949 #edb/ref 1065 1822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074949 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "833f94cb-00c4-54ac-9a66-7eaa2c22de12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074949 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
